{"name":"Tofino","hex":"#e6baa9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tofino","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A settlement on the west coast of Vancouver Island, British Columbia, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tofino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tofino","blocks":[{"text":"Tofino is a town of approximately 2,516 residents on the west coast of Vancouver Island in the Canadian province of British Columbia. The District of Tofino is located at the western terminus of Highway 4 on the tip of the Esowista Peninsula at the southern edge of Clayoquot Sound. It is situated in the traditional territory of the Tla-o-qui-aht First Nations, who have occupied Clayoquot Sound for thousands of years. European and American vessels began trading along this coast in the late eighteenth century, and permanent non-Indigenous settlement began in the 1890s; the community took the name Tofino, after nearby Tofino Inlet, in the early 1900s, and its post office opened in 1909. Tofino was incorporated as a municipality in 1932 and as a district in 1982."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Tofino.Vue_vers_l%27est.JPG/330px-Tofino.Vue_vers_l%27est.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tofino"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Sanddollaronbeachtofinokjfmartin.jpg/500px-Sanddollaronbeachtofinokjfmartin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Sanddollaronbeachtofinokjfmartin.jpg/1280px-Sanddollaronbeachtofinokjfmartin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Sanddollaronbeachtofinokjfmartin.jpg/500px-Sanddollaronbeachtofinokjfmartin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten